{"qid":"Q924","names":["Tanzania"],"title":"Tanzania","endonym":{"native":"United Republic of Tanzania","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The United Republic of Tanzania was formed on 26 April 1964 by the union of the newly independent mainland state of Tanganyika (independent 1961) and the revolutionary Zanzibar sultanate after its January 1964 revolution. Under Julius Nyerere, Tanzania pursued the Arusha Declaration's ujamaa socialist villagisation policy from 1967, restructuring rural society at significant economic cost; Nyerere also ordered the military intervention that overthrew Idi Amin's Uganda in 1979. Following Nyerere's retirement in 1985, Tanzania gradually liberalized its economy and in 1992 adopted multiparty democracy, developing into one of East Africa's more stable states while depending heavily on gold exports, tourism, and agricultural revenue.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Tanzania's national borders are precisely defined by colonial-era and post-independence international boundaries; internal administrative divisions are well documented in government and UN records.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Tanzania","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Tanzania"}],"britannica":"place/Tanzania","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Tanzania","rulers":[{"qid":"Q186525","name":"Julius Nyerere","start":1964,"end":1985,"image":"President Nyerere van Tanzania, koppen, Bestanddeelnr 928-2879 (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/President%20Nyerere%20van%20Tanzania%2C%20koppen%2C%20Bestanddeelnr%20928-2879%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"licen